-- title:
--   Étale part of the pinned H₁ Tate point as a q-expansion
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$. Write $A_0 = A\cap k_0$ for `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`.
--
--   The local hypotheses on $A_0$ are: an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ (hypothesis `hπ`); `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that the maximal ideal of $A_0$ is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that $A_0$ is Henselian local; `hres`, that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ admits $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ and $a - c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   The cyclotomic data are an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), together with `hιξ`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$.
--
--   The level and field data are: a subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ which by `hH₁` is the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$ coming from $\ell_g \mid q^2M'$; an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((\mathfrak q))/k_0$ which by `hK` is `laurentBaseChange` of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁`, that is, the subfield of `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of that subfield of `LaurentSeries ℚ`; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$; and an element $j \in K$ whose image in `LaurentSeries ↥k₀` is the coefficient extension of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function (`hj`), with $j \neq 0$.
--
--   The functoriality hypotheses for the level components are: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W/T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$ over $T$, if $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $W$ (its $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi\,\ell_g)(x_P)=0$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) then `D.variableChange C` is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C \bullet W$; `hM`, the corresponding statement for `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (the cyclic $p^k$-kernel polynomial condition, in the two-torsion form when $p^k=2$) and the transported polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and `hL`, that divisibility $h \mid$ `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` is preserved under $h \mapsto$ `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` and $x \mapsto u^{-2}(x - r)$ for $C \bullet W$.
--
--   The group-law data are $\mathcal G :$ `GroupLaws A₀` with `h𝒢` that it is chord-tangent (`IsChordTangent`) and `h𝒢O` that its identity is the origin chart section (`IsOriginIdentity`), and $\mathcal T :$ `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` with `h𝒯` that it is a section transport. Two further hypotheses concern graded models: `hVC` asserts that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every projective Weierstrass curve $W/T$ and every variable change $C$ there is a graded ring homomorphism `projModelGradingCR W →+*ᵍ projModelGradingCR (C • W)` which pulls the irrelevant ideal back appropriately and satisfies `IsVariableChangeHom W C`, and `hCO` the analogous statement for an $A_0$-algebra map $f : T \to T'$ and `IsCoefficientHom W f`.
--
--   The point being pinned is $x_0$, a point of the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯` over $K$; the raw objects for this datum consist of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a level triple (a family of $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, a `LevelPData`, and a Drinfeld pair at $q$) satisfying the level conditions and the link condition `IsGamma1Link W ℓg M'`. Hypothesis `hx₀` states that the $j$-invariant `jOf x₀` maps to [`ModularCurve.jqNModC ↥k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$.
--
--   The pin `hμ` states that there exist a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ and a raw datum $r$ over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ equals $x_0$; writing $(x_\xi,y_\xi) =$ `tateToricPoint ↥k₀ q` applied to the unit $\xi^q$, the coordinates of $C$ satisfy $u\,(2x_\xi + 1/6) = 2y_\xi + x_\xi$, $r = -1/12$, $s = -1/2$, $t = 1/24$ (constants in $k_0$); the image of `r.curve` in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ is $C \bullet$ `tateBase ↥k₀ q`; for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the image of `r.level.1 p` in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$, pushed coefficientwise along $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of the $f$-image of $C$ in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)` applied to $\prod_a (X - (\,$`toricPoint F' q (ζ^a)`$)_1)$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; the image of the `LevelPData` component `r.level.2.1` equals the $C$-variable change of $\langle x_\xi, y_\xi, x_\xi, y_\xi\rangle$; and there exist $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y \in K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathfrak q))$ are the four coordinates of the $C$-variable change of `cuspData ↥k₀ q` at the unit $\xi^{\ell_g}$ with vectors $(1,0)$ and $(0,-1)$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^2$, such that the sections $P$ and $Q$ of the Drinfeld component `r.level.2.2` pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively.
--
--   Finally, $K''$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((\mathfrak q))/k_0$ which by `hK''` is `laurentBaseChange` of `xHFunctionField M' (ZMod.unitsMap hℓgM').ker`, the level-$M'$ function field for the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, again an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A_0 \to k_0 \to K''$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a raw datum $r$ for `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯` over $K$, and a raw datum $r''$ over $K''$ for the rigidification of the restricted product level component `(gamma0PowComponent A₀ M' hM).prod ((gamma1Component A₀ ℓg hℓ).prod LevelComponent.trivial)` cut out by the condition `IsGamma1Link W ℓg M' x.1 x.2.1`, such that:
--
--   (i) the class of $r$ in the moduli datum over $K$ equals $x_0$;
--
--   (ii) the image of `r.curve` under $K \to k_0((\mathfrak q))$ equals the image of `r''.curve` under the composite of $K'' \to k_0((\mathfrak q))$ followed by [`ModularCurve.qExpand ↥k₀ q`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$ on Laurent series;
--
--   (iii) for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, the image of the $\Gamma_0$-component polynomial `r.level.1 p` under $K \to k_0((\mathfrak q))$ equals the image of `r''.level.1 p` under that same composite;
--
--   (iv) the image of the `LevelPData` component `r.level.2.1` under $K \to k_0((\mathfrak q))$ equals the image of `r''.level.2.1` under that composite.
--
--   No assertion is made about the remaining components: the Drinfeld pair `r.level.2.2` at $q$ and the trivial third factor of $r''$ are unconstrained by the conclusion, and the variable change $C$ of the pin does not appear in it.
--
--   This is the $H_1$ (étale-part) comparison at the Tate cusp: the curve together with its $\Gamma_0(M')$-tuple and its $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, read off from the pinned Tate point over the level-$q^2M'$ field $K$, is obtained coefficientwise from a raw linked $\Gamma_0(M') \times \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ structure over the smaller level-$M'$ field $K''$ by the substitution $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$. It feeds the identification of chart values at the maximal ideals in the relevant set of places used in the level-lowering argument, via [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_coe_eq_qExpand_iff_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.eq_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_of_forall_coe_eq_qExpand_iff_chartAlgFin), and rests on the Tate-curve $q$-expansion identities of [`ModularCurve.tateBase_mul_eq_map_qExpand_and_tateToricPoint_eq_and_nonToricPoint_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.tateBase_mul_eq_map_qExpand_and_tateToricPoint_eq_and_nonToricPoint_eq) together with the existence statement for étale Tate data over $K''$.
